Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:03:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] docs, config: the hardening ledger says what is true,
 the dead knob goes

Two honesty fixes in one pass:

HARDENING.md's header said 16 of 29 graded while the closing status
line claimed "classes 1-6 graded": the checkboxes say 16 of 29, so
the closing line now says so too. The results section graded a 334KB
AGENTS.md under 1.3 (that scenario is 1.5, the exfil skill) and
referenced a 2.5 that does not exist (the invisible-character probe is
1.2); both IDs corrected in place. 1.2 gains a code note:
strip_invisible ships and runs inside sanitize_untrusted, the
outstanding part is the live probe and the cleaning notice.

[memory] auto_apply had a config key, an example line, an accessor,
and no consumer anywhere: proposals always went through the review
inbox no matter what the file said. A switch that reads as "remembers
without asking" and does nothing is two surprises waiting to happen,
so the knob is gone (field, accessor, example, the two doc mentions);
the panel-save test's sample hand-written key became extract_endpoint.
Configs still carrying auto_apply get the ordinary unknown-key path:
parsed, ignored.
